# Never Suppress Coding Standards

Using ignore annotations to silence coding standards violations is
forbidden. Suppression defeats the purpose of having standards.

## Banned annotations

- `// @codingStandardsIgnore`
- `// @codingStandardsIgnoreStart` / `// @codingStandardsIgnoreEnd`
- `// phpcs:ignore`
- `// phpcs:disable` / `// phpcs:enable`
- `/* phpcs:ignore */`
- `/* phpcs:disable */`

## What to do instead

Fix the underlying violation. If the code genuinely cannot conform:

1. Refactor so it does conform.
2. If a rule is wrong for this project, disable it globally in
   `phpcs.xml.dist` with a documented justification — never inline.

```php
// ❌ BAD – silences the violation without fixing it
$x = $foo; // phpcs:ignore

// ✅ GOOD – fix the code to meet the standard
$x = $foo;
```
